# tl::expected, which every fallible operation in AmberEdit answers with.
# Header-only, so it is a build dependency and never a runtime one. In universe
# on jammy and noble, which the official Ubuntu images enable and a minimal
# chroot does not — std::expected would need C++23 and the floor is g++ 8.
               libexpected-dev,
# doctest for the test suite, which dh_auto_test runs. One package name on
# trixie, jammy and noble alike — unlike catch2, which trixie renamed.
               doctest-dev
